==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Nighthunter Saki''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Bad Blaster Saki''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Sharpshooter Saki is generally used for long-range sniping. Her attacks can hit up to 900 range, making her very capable at demolishing any backliners in her target traits. Due to her target-only ability, however, there aren't too many places to use her. Her average health and high speed can make her vulnerable without protection. Saki boasts an extremely short cooldown, so if you can get around her high deployment cost, you can accumulate extreme amounts of DPS, shredding her targets with terrifying ease.

Overall, Saki is a situational unit. Good protection (such as [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]) is important to unleash her full potential, since her blindspot is massive (500 range). This makes her use difficult without support, especially considering that while Reds and Zombies have their fair share of ranged attackers like [[Professor A.]] and [[Cadaver Bear]], many other lower-ranged threats, specifically zombies that burrow, can be a huge problem if they aren't dealt with properly.

==='''True Form'''===
Bad Blaster Saki changes her [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] targeting to [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] targeting and loses her [[Zombie Killer]] ability in exchange for Immune to Curse. While she can destroy Relic backliners such as [[Othom]], [[Loris]] and [[Lowkey]], she falters against high durability Relic frontliners like [[Oldhorn]] and [[Relic Bun-Bun]], who usually push too far into her blindspot and are better dealt with by crowd-control units. It is important to note that Saki only begins her attacks when enemies of her targeted traits enters her '''attack range''', making her difficult to use in stages like [[Young Cuttlefish]] without a proper setup.

==='''Talents'''===
Strong gives Saki a very large boost to her usability and has no downsides. It's recommended to get this as fast as possible, since it will increase her survivability, and her already high DPS skyrockets to 11.3k against Relics and 13.6k against Aliens.

Many of Saki's talents are about keeping your 6300¢ unit alive, so giving her Survive gives her more chances to reposition to let her dish out more damage. As with most resistances, Freeze Resist isn't very helpful, although it can be good at countering [[Henry]] in some stages—sadly, talents don't carry over to other forms, and since there are a surprisingly quite a few Red/Zombie levels with Henry in them, this limits her usefulness in those stages. With that being said, Saki's base health is lacking, so giving her extra health is useful to not get all her knockbacks used at once, and as she's primarily a DPS unit, increasing her damage is always useful—but before you go to stat upgrades, get Strong first, as it boosts both health and damage more than the individual upgrades could do themselves.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
'''[[Strengthen]]''' is perhaps the most notable Ultra Talent, simply due to its massive bonus (up to +100%) easily compounding with her extreme damage. However, like [[Furiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Ragelan Pasalan]], the '''[[Survive]]''' Talent must be maxed for it to function properly due to it activating at only 1% health, making it difficult to set up and sustain due to her lacking Wave or Surge Immunity for a not-so-spectacular payoff when there are enough funds and time to defend and spawn more copies of her instead.

'''[[Immune to Explosion]]''' is a questionable upgrade for the most part. It denies one way of reaching her in the back, but the only noteworthy enemies within her targets that utilize Explosions are [[Advent Stages|Brutal Advent]] bosses, specifically [[Poultrio]] and [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]]. It may be worth unlocking this Ultra Talent if you're struggling with either Advent significantly, but there's hardly a point to it otherwise.

'''Target Dark''' is quite dubious. While this is valuable on a Target Only unit and provides more options against such threats, most of them are hyper-aggressive melee pushers that can quickly invade her blindspot if left unchecked, and many accessible alternatives already exist for them.

==='''Orb'''===
Strong Against Up Relic, Dark or Aliens orb would be the best ones to put on her, as she is a specialist for all of these traits, assuming you have unlocked her "Strong Against" talent. Note that these orbs won't carry over to other forms.

Two S-Tier Wave/Surge Resist Orbs can also be used to negate her vulnerability to one or the other.

